BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:'Museum Reads' Book Club at Newport Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260821
DTSTAMP:20260820T110130Z
UID:239fbc54aa52999f6e8040e9ceb5@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Museum Reads\, the Newport Art Museum’s Art-Theme
 d book group for adults! Are you looking to learn more about art and artis
 ts\, or enjoy digging into some of the issues present in our current exhib
 itions? Then this friendly discussion group is for you. We meet monthly on
  the third Thursday at 12:00 PM\, in person and virtually. Join us virtual
 ly from the office for an invigorating lunch break or enjoy an hour of ins
 piration during a wee one’s nap time or find us in the gallery for in-pe
 rson conversation. Upcoming Dates: April 16 - Stand and Gus: Art\, Ardor\,
  and the Friendship That Built the Gilded Age May 14 - Murder at Arleigh J
 une 18 - Surreal: The Extraordinary Life of Gala Dali July 16 - Jamestown:
  Architecture\, Landscape\, and the Making of a Rhode Paradise August 20 -
  A Month in Siena September 17 - Mary Cassatt between Paris and New York: 
 The Making of a Transatlantic Legacy October 15 - Winslow Homer: American 
 Passage Museum Reads is free for Members\, and $5 for yet-to-be Members. B
 e sure to register online to receive email updates and Zoom links. For las
 t minute registrations\, please call the front desk for the Zoom link at 4
 01-848-8200.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/museum-read
 s-book-club-at-newport-art-museum/109609/
LOCATION:Newport Art Museum\, 76 Bellevue Avenue\, Newport\, RI 02840
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/museum-reads-book-club-at-newpo
 rt-art-museum/109609/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Newport National Security Dinner
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260821
DTSTAMP:20260820T110130Z
UID:9dcc9dcbecc14177d7c6b210e746@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:2026 Newport National Security Dinner When: Thursday\, August 
 20th from 6:00 to 10:00 PM Where: Gardiner House\, 24 Lee's Wharf\, Newpor
 t Join the Naval War College Foundation for the Newport National Security 
 Dinner\, presented by Peter and Jennifer Scanlon\, on Thursday\, August 20
 \, the eve of the Newport National Security Symposium. This exclusive even
 ing brings together senior military leaders\, national security experts\, 
 business executives\, policymakers\, and supporters of the Naval War Colle
 ge Foundation and the U.S. Naval War College for meaningful conversation a
 nd connection. Set against the backdrop of Newport Harbor at the award-win
 ning Gardiner House\, guests will enjoy a cocktail reception and seated di
 nner while engaging with leaders shaping the future of global security and
  strategic leadership. As the premier networking event surrounding the Sym
 posium\, the Dinner offers a unique opportunity to build relationships and
  exchange ideas before the Newport National Security Symposium convenes on
  Friday\, August 21\, at the U.S. Naval War College. Learn more\, explore 
 sponsorship opportunities\, and register at https://nwcfoundation.org/nnsd
 inner.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/2026-newport-nati
 onal-security-dinner/111303/
